instructions.dataflow_inspector:
Carefully inspect the entire code script to find every line that references the target column. Look for exact string matches of the column name in indexing (e.g., df['col']), attribute access, column lists (e.g., out_cols, select, drop), sorting operations (sort_values), filters, transformations, merges, joins, index sets, and output export statements.

Use 1-based line numbers. Group contiguous lines into a single range. Ensure no occurrences (especially in final output column definitions or export calls) are missed.

Output only JSON: { "sources": [{ "start_line": int, "end_line": int }, ...] }

